{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Random|class Seed|next\\\\(\\\\).*number|random\\\\(\\\\)' API.md | head -15 && sed -n '4469,4495p' API.md && sed -n '3587,3609p' API.md && head -50 CREDITS.md\"","aggregated_output":"4665:- `next(): number`: Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32.\n### class Mirror\n\n- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera is behind the glass.\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface MirrorOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.\n- `tintAmount?: number`\n\n### class NavGrid\n\n- `new NavGrid(width: number, height: number, o: NavGridOptions = {})`\n- `static fromRows(rows: readonly string[], o: NavGridOptions & { blocked?: string } = {}): NavGrid`: From an ASCII map: `blocked` characters are closed, everything else open. Default '# ': walls and pits (a ' ' has no floor in RoomKit's maps); past the end of a short row is a wall.\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n- `readonly cell: number`\n- `readonly ox: number`: World x, z of cell (0, 0)'s corner.\n- `readonly oz: number`\n- `readonly open: Uint8Array`: 1 = walkable.\n### compileClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClip(def: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec, rest: RestPose): AnimationClip\n```\n\nBake a ClipDef into a three.js AnimationClip (quaternion + position + scale tracks,\nsampled at 60 Hz so easing and per-axis Euler interpolation — including 360° flips —\nsurvive exactly).\n\n### compileClips()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\n```\n\n### interface Foot\n\n- `readonly at: Vec3`: World position of the foot now.\n- `t: number`: Stepping: 0 → 1 through the step; -1 planted.\n- `readonly from: Vec3`\n- `readonly to: Vec3`\n\n# Credits (Pixel Engine 0.46.0)\n\nWhat this kit carries and where it came from, generated by `npm run bundle` from each built-in model's and texture's `source` (the data the engine repository's `npm run model -- credits` reads) and from the bundled packages' own licence files. Ship this file with a game built on the kit.\n\n## Models and textures\n\n- **The engine's own work**, made in its repository: 151 of the 151 library models (`MODEL_LIBRARY`), 126 of the 126 textures (`TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/hero.glb`, `assets/tree.glb`). Nothing to credit.\n- **kenney-castle** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/castle-kit/a395102d20-1711543616/kenney_castle-kit.zip. Models: kenney-castle/bridge-draw, kenney-castle/bridge-straight-pillar, kenney-castle/bridge-straight, kenney-castle/door, kenney-castle/flag-banner-long, kenney-castle/flag-banner-short, kenney-castle/flag-pennant, kenney-castle/flag-wide, kenney-castle/flag, kenney-castle/gate, kenney-castle/ground-hills, kenney-castle/ground, kenney-castle/metal-gate, kenney-castle/rocks-large, kenney-castle/rocks-small, kenney-castle/siege-ballista-demolished, kenney-castle/siege-ballista, kenney-castle/siege-catapult-demolished, kenney-castle/siege-catapult, kenney-castle/siege-ram-demolished, kenney-castle/siege-ram, kenney-castle/siege-tower-demolished, kenney-castle/siege-tower, kenney-castle/siege-trebuchet-demolished, kenney-castle/siege-trebuchet, kenney-castle/stairs-stone-square, kenney-castle/stairs-stone, kenney-castle/tower-base, kenney-castle/tower-hexagon-base, kenney-castle/tower-hexagon-mid, kenney-castle/tower-hexagon-roof-secondary, kenney-castle/tower-hexagon-roof, kenney-castle/tower-hexagon-top-wood, kenney-castle/tower-hexagon-top, kenney-castle/tower-slant-roof, kenney-castle/tower-square-arch, kenney-castle/tower-square-base-border, kenney-castle/tower-square-base-color, kenney-castle/tower-square-base, kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-color, kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-door, kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-open-simple, kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-open, kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-windows, kenney-castle/tower-square-mid, kenney-castle/tower-square-roof, kenney-castle/tower-square-top-color, kenney-castle/tower-square-top-roof-high-windows, kenney-castle/tower-square-top-roof-high, kenney-castle/tower-square-top-roof-rounded, kenney-castle/tower-square-top-roof, kenney-castle/tower-square-top, kenney-castle/tower-square, kenney-castle/tower-top, kenney-castle/tree-large, kenney-castle/tree-log, kenney-castle/tree-small, kenney-castle/tree-trunk, kenney-castle/wall-corner-half-tower, kenney-castle/wall-corner-half, kenney-castle/wall-corner-slant, kenney-castle/wall-corner, kenney-castle/wall-doorway, kenney-castle/wall-half-modular, kenney-castle/wall-half, kenney-castle/wall-narrow-corner, kenney-castle/wall-narrow-gate, kenney-castle/wall-narrow-stairs-rail, kenney-castle/wall-narrow-stairs, kenney-castle/wall-narrow-wood-fence, kenney-castle/wall-narrow-wood, kenney-castle/wall-narrow, kenney-castle/wall-pillar, kenney-castle/wall-stud, kenney-castle/wall-to-narrow, kenney-castle/wall.\n- **kenney-furniture** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/