{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -A 22 '\"'^### renderSheet|''^### interface Sheet|''^### interface RenderSheet|''^### interface ClipSheet|''^### interface PosedSheet'\"' API.md && rg -n -A 22 '\"'^### modelSheet'\"' API.md && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('check/tests.json')\nif p.exists():\n d=json.loads(p.read_text());print('Last completed run:', d['passed'], '/', d['passed']+d['failed'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"3375:### interface SheetImport\n3376-\n3377-- `readonly defs: readonly TextureDef[]`\n3378-- `readonly colours: readonly SheetColour[]`: Every distinct opaque source colour of the imported cells, biggest first.\n3379-- `readonly merges: readonly SheetMerge[]`: Every PALETTE entry two or more of those colours bake as, biggest first.\n3380-- `readonly map: ColourMap`: The mapper's result (slots and their entries, before `palette` re-binds them).\n3381-- `readonly cells: readonly SheetCell[]`: Every cell of the grid, in reading order.\n3382-- `readonly columns: number`\n3383-- `readonly rows: number`\n3384-\n3385:### interface SheetImportOptions\n3386-\n3387-- `readonly as: string`: The ids' prefix (`IMPORT_ID`: `tiles`, `kit/tiles`): cells are `<as>-<index>` (or `<as>-<name>`), a strip of frames is `<as>`.\n3388-- `readonly grid: readonly [w: number, h: number]`: A cell's size in pixels, width × height; the sheet must be whole cells.\n3389-- `readonly source: Omit<Provenance, 'tool' | 'colours' | 'fidelity'>`: What the caller knows of the source (url, licence, pack, file, author, sha256); the import adds `tool` and `colours`.\n3390-- `readonly tile?: boolean`: The cells are surfaces that tile: each def gets `tile: true` (the check measures the seam).\n3391-- `readonly frames?: boolean`: One def of frames, left to right, from the cells in reading order (an animation strip).\n3392-- `readonly cells?: readonly number[]`: Cells to import by index, in reading order (row by row from the top; default every cell).\n3393-- `readonly names?: readonly string[]`: Names by cell index, in reading order: cell `i` becomes `<as>-<names[i]>` ('' keeps the index).\n3394-- `readonly alpha?: number`: Alpha (0–255) under which a pixel is transparent (default `ALPHA_THRESHOLD`).\n3395-- `readonly palette?: Readonly<Record<TexSlot, PaletteColor>>`: Slots re-bound after mapping, for every def at once: `{ c3: 'sand' }`.\n3396-- `readonly tags?: readonly string[]`\n3397-\n3398-### spriteSheet()\n3399-\n3400-```ts\n3401-function spriteSheet(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, opts: TextureOptions = {}): SpriteSheet\n3402-```\n3403-\n3404-A sprite sheet for `SpriteBatch`: the def's frames left to right in one row, rows stored top\n3405-first (`flipY` false, which SpriteBatch reads). Not cached: a SpriteBatch disposes its sheet.\n3406-\n3407-### TEXTURE_FAMILIES\n--\n3756:### renderSheet()\n3757-\n3758-```ts\n3759-function renderSheet(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip, options: SheetOptions = {}): SheetImage\n3760-```\n3761-\n3762-Render a contact sheet for one clip.\n3763-\n3764-### interface RigSpec\n3765-\n3766-Everything the tools need to know about a rig beyond its hierarchy.\n3767-\n3768-- `joints: readonly string[]`: Joint names in hierarchy order (root first).\n3769-- `root: string`\n3770-- `mirror: Readonly<Record<string, string>>`: Left/right counterparts for mirroring.\n3771-- `soles: readonly string[]`: Mesh names that touch the ground (soles).\n3772-- `trace: readonly string[]`: Points to trace in contact sheets (joint or mesh names).\n3773-- `limits: Readonly<Record<string, JointLimit>>`: Human-plausible rotation ranges, degrees.\n3774-- `fps: number`: Frame rate of the authoring format.\n3775-- `legs?: LegRig`: Leg geometry, enabling foot IK and the gait generator.\n3776-- `spine?: { torso?: string; head?: string; cap?: string }`: Joints the runtime procedural layers turn (PoseLayers): the torso and head look where the character is going; `cap` is an optional springy joint (not animated by clips).\n3777-\n3778-### sampleClip()\n--\n3787:### interface SheetImage\n3788-\n3789-Tiny RGBA software canvas shared by contact sheets, curve plots and filmstrips (no GPU, no DOM).\n3790-\n3791-- `width: number`\n3792-- `height: number`\n3793-- `data: Uint8ClampedArray`\n3794-\n3795-### class SpringChain\n3796-\n3797-A chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\n3798-with the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\n3799-then read `points` (root first).\n3800-\n3801-- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n3802-- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n3803-- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n3804-- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n3805-- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n3806-- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n3807-\n3808-### interface SpringChainOptions\n3809-\n3205:### modelSheet()\n3206-\n3207-```ts\n3208-function modelSheet(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelSheetOptions = {}): ModelSheet\n3209-```\n3210-\n3211-The model sheet `npm run model -- sheet` draws, for a library id or any def (a game's own):\n3212-the turntable, front / side / top on a 0.1 m grid with the size, the game-scale previews, the\n3213-palette and `checkModel`'s problems and warnings over every param's range. Software-drawn: no\n3214-GPU, no DOM, so it runs in Node and in a browser (the kit's `check.mjs --sheets`). A def that\n3215-can't be built (an unknown slot, `use` or texture) gets a sheet of its problems alone.\n3216-\n3217-  const { image, problems } = modelSheet(myStall, { catalog: myModels }); // image: RGBA pixels\n3218-\n3219-### interface ModelSheet\n3220-\n3221-A model's sheet (`image`: width, height and RGBA `data`) and the check it shows.\n3222-\n3223-- `readonly image: SheetImage`\n3224-- `readonly problems: readonly string[]`\n3225-- `readonly warnings: readonly string[]`\n3226-- `readonly report: ModelReport | null`: Tris, draws, materials, parts (null when it can't be built).\n3227-- `readonly bounds: Bounds | null`: Its bounds in metres: min, max and size (null when it can't be built).\nLast completed run: 87 / 88\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
