{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_100","type":"agent_message","text":"The full run passed **113/113 checks**, including the engine’s package check and all four Hub cases. A final check found that hub and Medley music also needed to resume after pause; I’ve fixed that and added a test. I’m writing the feedback into About and the exit interview, then rebuilding the hand-in files.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_101","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/data/about.js');s=p.read_text()\na=s.index(' testingFeedback:');b=s.index('\\\\n aiHub:',a)\ns=s[:a]+''' testingFeedback:['22 functional and visual issues were caught and corrected, grouping related symptoms as one issue.','Two could block a flow: a scene-transition/voice race, and starting Family Hour with only a controller.','The real-menu seven-day playthrough, followed by browser pad, viewport, audio and four Hub harness runs.','Title-only smoke checks gave little coverage of the story, multiple devices, pause or resized HUD.'],\n engineFeedback:['Data-authored models and clips, the pixel renderer and the shared headless runtime made a complete game practical.','I first analyzed clips on a posed model. A neutral rig exposed two foot-placement errors. Menu time also needed the unscaled replay delta.','The unstable Dot, shared activity rules/drivers, controller HUD and persistent week/story framework.','Coordinating asynchronous scene loads, fixed-step gameplay, paused UI time, animation feet and manual WebGPU captures.','None. The shipped pixel-engine.js is byte-identical to the downloaded 0.46.0 kit.','Expose unscaled UI frame time directly on GameContext.'],\n promptFeedback:['The clear tone, four pillars, exact mechanics and verified engine/Hub recipes gave the game a strong direction.','The brief asks for a vertical slice while the plan describes a whole week and seventeen activities.','Keeping all activities, controller/keyboard/mouse controls, story progression and online sessions consistent and readable.','Separate core acceptance criteria from optional polish, while keeping the verified recipes and testing stand-ins.'],\n'''+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
